  "content": "\\[\nP(x)=x^5-x^2+5=\\prod_{k=1}^5(x-x_k)\n\\]\n\nThen\n\\[\n\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k^2+1)=\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k-i)\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k+i)\n\\]\n\nSince\n\\[\nP(i)=\\prod_{k=1}^5(i-x_k)=(-1)^5\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k-i),\n\\]\nso\n\\[\n\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k-i)=-P(i).\n\\]\nSimilarly,\n\\[\n\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k+i)=-P(-i).\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\n\\prod_{k=1}^5(x_k^2+1)=P(i)P(-i).\n\\]\n\nNow\n\\[\nP(i)=i^5-i^2+5=i+1+5=6+i,\n\\]\n\\[\nP(-i)=(-i)^5-(-i)^2+5=-i+1+5=6-i.\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[\nP(i)P(-i)=(6+i)(6-i)=36+1=37.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{37}\n\\]",
